WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.400
Pick ten leaves from one white oak.

2
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.620
Every leaf has rounded lobes.

3
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:15.300
But measure them with a ruler, and you will almost surely find different lengths and shapes.

4
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.020
So why is no living thing exactly like another?

5
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.640
And are all mutations bad?

6
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:29.223
A trait is a feature of a living thing, such as color, shape or height.

7
00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:34.823
A population is a group of the same kind of living thing in one area.

8
00:00:35.743 --> 00:00:38.923
Members of a population share the same basic features.

9
00:00:39.363 --> 00:00:42.183
But each one varies a little in every trait.

10
00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:45.283
Variation means these small differences.

11
00:00:46.283 --> 00:00:48.883
Some variation comes from genes.

12
00:00:49.723 --> 00:00:52.103
A gene carries the code for a protein.

13
00:00:53.103 --> 00:00:55.303
Some variation comes from the environment.

14
00:00:56.403 --> 00:00:57.403
Height shows both.

15
00:00:58.423 --> 00:01:00.363
Many genes add a little to height.

16
00:01:01.403 --> 00:01:03.923
Food and health during childhood matter too.

17
00:01:04.743 --> 00:01:08.923
So two children with very similar genes can grow to different heights.

18
00:01:09.867 --> 00:01:12.747
New variation starts with a mutation.

19
00:01:13.707 --> 00:01:18.447
A mutation is a change in the DNA sequence, the order of the bases.

20
00:01:19.327 --> 00:01:22.007
It can change the protein a gene codes for.

21
00:01:23.027 --> 00:01:27.347
Copying mistakes, radiation, or some chemicals can cause mutations.

22
00:01:28.487 --> 00:01:29.887
Mutations are random.

23
00:01:30.907 --> 00:01:35.287
Random means they happen by chance, not because a living thing needs them.

24
00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:38.830
Where a mutation happens matters.

25
00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:45.450
Body cells are all the cells of the body except eggs and sperm, such as skin cells.

26
00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:48.330
Sex cells are eggs and sperm.

27
00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.530
A mutation in a skin cell stays in that person.

28
00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.570
A mutation in a sex cell can pass to offspring, the young.

29
00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.143
Does a mutation help?

30
00:01:59.883 --> 00:02:03.023
That depends on the living thing and where it lives.

31
00:02:03.963 --> 00:02:05.843
Think of a misprint in a recipe.

32
00:02:06.663 --> 00:02:08.243
Most misprints change little.

33
00:02:08.923 --> 00:02:10.183
Some ruin the dish.

34
00:02:10.823 --> 00:02:12.663
A rare one makes it better.

35
00:02:13.403 --> 00:02:17.583
But a recipe has a writer, and no one chooses a mutation.

36
00:02:18.443 --> 00:02:21.943
A mutation can help, harm or make no difference.

37
00:02:22.643 --> 00:02:25.003
So not all mutations are bad.
